A||N||2||Scott_M||Can't find Reverse ||||5||
Z||000000||Scott_M||06-24-2000||08:41 PM||||I have an 87' SE 4 cyl 2.5L.,that had a new clutch put in 96' when it wouldn’t shift out of 2nd. This week, after replacing the brake pads on all four wheels I decided to top off the manual transaxle fluid level because it had started getting hard to shift. I took off the speedometer sensor as the manual said (noticing a puff of pressurized air escaping as it came off) and filled it with SAE 5w-30 oil. Now I can't find reverse, and gears 1-5 are all over the place. I was able to go around the block thinking it might work itself out. But the problem remains. I can't even get the reverse lights to come on. The clutch master cyl is full/dry, with no leaks.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||06-24-2000||10:30 PM||||Welcome, Scott    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Sounds like when it started getting hard to shift, you forced things, to where the shift cable adjusting nuts slipped in their slots on the levers on top of the transaxle.  <P>Strictly a guess, mind you    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !  I really shouldn't go around accusing people I don't even know!   <P>There should be no relative movement between the (2) shift cable ends and the levers on top of the transmission.  These are on LHS of the engine compartment; two big cables that arch over from centerline of eng. compartment, make a big rainbow arch over to LHS of transaxle.  The cables attach with nuts, to slotted holes in the levers on the top of the transaxle.<P>If the nuts are loose, then you'll know why the gears are "all over the place."<P>The puff of air from the transaxle I really don't know about, but it doesn't sound good...<P>I think you have an Isuzu 5-speed in your car, the transmission I know least about. <P>Anyway, first try adjusting the linkage.<P>        <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-24-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000002||Scott_M||06-25-2000||04:46 PM||||It was the cable. When I was refilling the transaxle I must have knocked off the ball joint connector. It went back on with a snap. No more problems. At least shifting that is! <BR>thx<BR>mark||||reg||1
